# The vehicle on the flight map, drawn as Mission Planner's marker for its type - ported from
# Common.getMAVMarker and ExtLibs/Maps/GMapMarkerQuad.cs - after the owner's report of 2026-10-02
# that it was a red arrow "that looks like a mouse cursor, not like a quadcopter or plane or rover".
#
# The claim: SITL's copter (MAV_TYPE QUADROTOR, sysid 1) is a GMapMarkerQuad (Common.cs:188-215):
# four motors and arms turned to cs.yaw, its sysid beside it, and from its point the heading line
# (red), the course (black) and its Target - cs.nav_bearing - (orange), each GMapMarkerBase.length
# long; a quad draws no nav-bearing line (GMapMarkerQuad.cs:132-149). With no settings written the
# Planner page's GMapMarkerBase_Display* are all on (MainV2.cs:3862-3867). The heading is the
# marker's Heading, cs.yaw, as degrees from 0 to 360.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-map-marker.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 7

expect vehicle.count > 0
expect map.ready true
expect map.vehicle.kind quad
expect map.vehicle.sysid 1
expect map.vehicle.lines heading,cog,target
expect map.vehicle.heading >= 0
expect map.vehicle.heading < 360
